      "value": "@{5d359d69973cc81d91d41ee4|full_name}: not to mention, the overhead introduced for doing it that way would be quite a bit, and seeing as the team mentioned worrying about the extra overhead in their video, I think this would be a good case to think about.  Unfortunately I can't go try those things myself atm as my computer died yesterday while uploading, but I think adding a \"Vector3.Magnitude\" can just not happen if the parameter isn't there to drive right? Also it would be much more performant that way than attempting to do it in the animator.",
